      "content": "thanks for the suggestion. i've been looking into those faraday bags, but i'm worried a bag for my phone won't be enough if they're using lower frequency waves that penetrate much deeper. do you think there are specific materials, like heavy lead shielding or even certain types of copper mesh, that are better at stopping infrasonic or low-frequency waves from reaching my head? and is there a way to tell if the frequency they're using is being modulated to match my own brainwaves?",
